  "notes": "USAGE: The standard term used in news reports and legal contexts for a person suspected of a crime. Japanese media follows strict terminology conventions depending on the stage of legal proceedings.\n\nLEGAL TERMINOLOGY PROGRESSION:\n- {容疑者|ようぎしゃ}: suspect (before charges are filed)\n- {被疑者|ひぎしゃ}: suspect (formal legal term, same stage)\n- {被告人|ひこくにん}: defendant (after charges are filed)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {容疑者|ようぎしゃ}を{逮捕|たいほ}する: to arrest a suspect\n- {容疑者|ようぎしゃ}を{特定|とくてい}する: to identify a suspect\n- {容疑者|ようぎしゃ}の{身柄|みがら}を{確保|かくほ}する: to take a suspect into custody",
